1
00:01:45,479 --> 00:01:47,440
Why are you tapping on it?

2
00:01:48,445 --> 00:01:52,738
Doing this tells me where the
wood is rotten or eaten by bugs.

3
00:01:52,856 --> 00:01:53,795
Bugs?

4
00:01:54,249 --> 00:01:55,760
Wood-eating bugs.

5
00:02:02,139 --> 00:02:04,191
Oops, found one.

6
00:02:05,926 --> 00:02:07,246
Look here.

7
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:09,100
Ugh, gross!

8
00:02:10,470 --> 00:02:13,480
All right, then let's burn this piece.

9
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:18,245
What happens if we just leave it?

10
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:22,600
When heavy rain fills the pond, 
the sluice gate will break.

11
00:02:23,174 --> 00:02:25,400
Hmm, why would it break?

12
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:27,320
From the water pressure.

13
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:32,180
Pressure is incredible. But just
one tiny hole should be fine, right?

14
00:02:32,454 --> 00:02:37,320
No, no. As the saying goes, even a massive
levee can collapse from a single ant hole.

15
00:02:37,765 --> 00:02:38,897
What does that mean?

16
00:02:39,322 --> 00:02:43,169
It means even a sturdy
dike can be destroyed...

17
00:02:43,193 --> 00:02:45,392
...starting from one little ant hole.

18
00:03:05,430 --> 00:03:07,860
Always be careful, even with little things.

19
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:11,280
That's terrible. Then
everything would be flooded!

20
00:03:12,114 --> 00:03:14,220
Indeed. And that's not all.

21
00:03:14,445 --> 00:03:20,420
If the reservoir empties, crops won't grow,
and we won't have drinking water either.

22
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:23,920
Oh no, that's awful! I'll help you too.

23
00:03:25,783 --> 00:03:26,298
Here.

24
00:03:27,015 --> 00:03:30,340
Thank you. You're such a kind boy.

25
00:03:36,410 --> 00:03:38,254
Hey Mokku!

26
00:03:38,738 --> 00:03:40,332
Mokku!

27
00:03:40,816 --> 00:03:42,941
Over here! Over here!

28
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,560
Why are you calling Mokku?

29
00:03:46,165 --> 00:03:49,020
You don't get it? We're gonna use him.

30
00:03:49,364 --> 00:03:50,489
Use him how?

31
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:52,060
The water's still cold, right?

32
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:56,074
So we put Mokku in the
water to flush out the fish.

33
00:03:56,390 --> 00:03:58,835
Oh, I see. Good idea.

34
00:03:59,255 --> 00:04:03,114
We're catching fish!
It's fun! Come over here!

35
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:06,778
Fish? What should I do?

36
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:08,905
I'm going!

37
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,898
Hey, Mokku!

38
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:14,795
Wait! I'm coming!

39
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,441
Hopeless boy.

40
00:04:17,473 --> 00:04:19,213
He's only interested in playing.

41
00:04:23,098 --> 00:04:25,646
All right, do your best! Did it slip away?

42
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:30,238
Go! Get 'em, get 'em, get 'em!

43
00:04:31,723 --> 00:04:33,301
Get 'em, get 'em!

44
00:04:51,117 --> 00:04:52,594
We did it!

45
00:05:01,022 --> 00:05:03,875
Phew, I'm exhausted!
Man, look, that's carp!

46
00:05:03,899 --> 00:05:05,679
The smell is incredible.

47
00:05:05,977 --> 00:05:08,257
Look how plump it is! Let's
cook those bad boys up!

48
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:12,250
Honestly, my mouth is drooling
like crazy. I wonder why...

49
00:05:12,757 --> 00:05:15,160
A fresh carp washed-sashimi,
ready to serve, baby!

50
00:05:15,236 --> 00:05:17,140
Whoa, now you're talking, Boss!

51
00:05:17,164 --> 00:05:20,273
You sure know your stuff when it
comes to good snacks, so no wonder
you know your way around cooking!

52
00:05:20,297 --> 00:05:23,580
A bit of fresh carp sashimi...
I can't resist! I wonder why...

53
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:31,984
Idiot! I'm starving! That lunch of yours
didn't fill me up at all! Look at this!

54
00:05:34,716 --> 00:05:35,760
I'm sorry, Boss.

55
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:37,920
All right, go swipe that carp!

56
00:05:37,979 --> 00:05:41,743
W-What? No, I can't! At night
maybe, but in broad daylight...

57
00:05:43,429 --> 00:05:48,560
You slow-witted fool. You've got a weasel's
last trick—a real good stinker—don't you?

58
00:05:48,855 --> 00:05:53,500
But, Boss, that's what you use when
you're running away. I wonder why.

59
00:05:54,423 --> 00:05:56,688
What do you mean "I wonder why"?! 
You distract them with a stink...

60
00:05:56,712 --> 00:05:59,147
...powerful enough to rip their
nose off, and that's your chance!

61
00:05:59,315 --> 00:06:01,250
Hey, brilliant!

62
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,560
Ready?

63
00:06:18,529 --> 00:06:19,175
Stand by!

64
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,480
Ready to go?

65
00:06:23,415 --> 00:06:26,140
Gotta go! Gotta go! Gotta go!

66
00:06:32,909 --> 00:06:33,807
He did it!

67
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:58,840
Boss, it's the wind's fault! It's the wind!

68
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:00,000
I wonder why.

69
00:07:02,049 --> 00:07:03,336
Swish, swish, swish!

70
00:07:04,431 --> 00:07:05,795
Get outta here! Shoo!

71
00:07:14,850 --> 00:07:16,400
It came off!

72
00:07:17,105 --> 00:07:18,883
It's detached!

73
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,540
What's this? A wood bug?

74
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:29,480
Huh? It looks just like
the bugs at the sluice gate!

75
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,240
I see, it washed down here.

76
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:35,817
Unbelievable, trying to eat my foot.

77
00:07:46,501 --> 00:07:50,220
Did the bugs eat away at it and mess up
the measurements where his knee moves?

78
00:07:50,321 --> 00:07:51,602
Could have.

79
00:08:00,992 --> 00:08:03,076
Can you even walk like that?!

80
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:04,330
I think so, but...

81
00:08:09,131 --> 00:08:10,210
This is weird...

82
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,116
He's broken! He's broken!

83
00:08:21,590 --> 00:08:23,178
Let's go! Let's go! Let's go home!

84
00:08:23,329 --> 00:08:23,894


85
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,809
Damn that Franco!

86
00:08:27,350 --> 00:08:29,120
Grandpa will make me a new one!

87
00:08:56,303 --> 00:08:58,478
All done. Here is your new leg.

88
00:08:58,503 --> 00:08:59,886
Cool!

89
00:09:00,221 --> 00:09:02,512
It's the exact same size as the old one.

90
00:09:03,269 --> 00:09:04,985
Here, let me attach it for you.

91
00:09:08,165 --> 00:09:11,946
Well, no one will laugh
at you now. Try walking.

92
00:09:12,298 --> 00:09:13,540
Thank you, Grandpa.

93
00:09:17,510 --> 00:09:18,469
What is the matter?

94
00:09:20,129 --> 00:09:21,280
I tripped.

95
00:09:27,749 --> 00:09:28,980
Your leg won't move.

96
00:09:39,905 --> 00:09:40,905
Mokku!

97
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,240
Grandpa, why did you
make me a leg like this?!

98
00:09:47,810 --> 00:09:50,065
I want a leg that moves like before!

99
00:09:50,595 --> 00:09:52,740
B-But even if you say that...

100
00:09:52,939 --> 00:09:56,003
Grandpa has no idea
why it won't move either...

101
00:10:36,590 --> 00:10:37,840
How nice...

102
00:10:38,139 --> 00:10:40,960
When everyone else plays in the
river, they don't get wood bugs...

103
00:10:41,309 --> 00:10:44,452
Even if they get muddy,
they're fine once they wash off!

104
00:10:45,919 --> 00:10:48,031
And yet, I'm...

105
00:10:52,289 --> 00:10:57,867
I hate this... I hate it! I don't
want to be a puppet anymore!

106
00:11:02,319 --> 00:11:03,790
M-Mokku...

107
00:11:26,002 --> 00:11:30,620
Don't you get it? Even if it's
made from fine oak, it won't move.

108
00:11:34,569 --> 00:11:37,315
Not without the Oak Tree Fairy's power.

109
00:11:45,604 --> 00:11:47,222
Aaah... I'm so hungry!

110
00:11:47,247 --> 00:11:50,605
I've got to eat somehow! I wonder why.

111
00:11:50,629 --> 00:11:56,120
Man, I want to eat carp. I've gotta
eat carp somehow. I want to eat carp.

112
00:11:57,135 --> 00:11:59,485
Wait! I've got a great idea!

113
00:12:00,274 --> 00:12:02,193
Jackpot! Time to eat!

114
00:12:02,455 --> 00:12:05,073
Huh? A master who can make legs that move?

115
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:07,480
Shh! Keep your voice down!

116
00:12:07,595 --> 00:12:10,600
That's right! There's a
master leg-maker around!

117
00:12:10,875 --> 00:12:12,696
W-Where is this master?

118
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:14,524
You want us to tell you?

119
00:12:14,749 --> 00:12:15,820
Please!

120
00:12:17,790 --> 00:12:20,435
I could tell you, but not for free!

121
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:21,781
Yeah!

122
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:24,440
What do you mean? What should I do?

123
00:12:24,930 --> 00:12:29,080
Oh, nothing much. Just lend us
a hand for a bit. Simple as that.

124
00:12:52,059 --> 00:12:53,720
Even this is better than
not being able to move.

125
00:12:56,689 --> 00:12:58,640
Mokku, what are you doing?

126
00:12:59,425 --> 00:13:00,425
I'm leaving.

127
00:13:02,170 --> 00:13:03,360
Leaving? Where to?

128
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:06,090
Leave me alone. What does it matter where?

129
00:13:19,359 --> 00:13:21,680
Fine. If you want to know
that badly, I'll tell you.

130
00:13:22,309 --> 00:13:25,069
I'm going to a master
puppet maker who's way...

131
00:13:25,093 --> 00:13:28,460
...way better than Grandpa,
to have him make me a leg!

132
00:13:28,665 --> 00:13:30,085
Much better?

133
00:13:30,633 --> 00:13:31,153
That's right.

134
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,512
There's no master like that.

135
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:34,800
Yes, there is!

136
00:13:35,145 --> 00:13:38,594
Nobody anywhere can make a
puppet that moves like a real human.

137
00:13:38,640 --> 00:13:39,995
Yes, there is!

138
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:41,940
There really is! I heard all about him!

139
00:13:42,735 --> 00:13:43,800
No, there isn't.

140
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:48,344
Goodbye.

141
00:13:50,939 --> 00:13:51,743
Mokku!

142
00:14:17,379 --> 00:14:21,040
Hmm, having legs that
won't move must be tough.

143
00:14:21,310 --> 00:14:23,580
Come on, tell me. What
do you want me to do?

144
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:29,820
It's simple, really. Just catch two or
three fish from this reservoir for me.

145
00:14:30,075 --> 00:14:34,387
Catch them? How, without any tools?

146
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:41,783
It's a piece of cake. Look, you just
open this floodgate and drain the water.

147
00:14:41,807 --> 00:14:43,960
Then you can just grab 'em with
your bare hands without any gear.

148
00:14:44,109 --> 00:14:48,087
All right, I'll try. But in return,
once I catch the fish, you have to...

149
00:14:48,539 --> 00:14:50,000
I'm tellin' ya, you can move it!

150
00:14:53,170 --> 00:14:55,549
Good boy, good boy. We
don't have to lift a finger...

151
00:14:55,573 --> 00:14:58,460
...and we can eat all
we want, that's how it is.

152
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:03,860
As expected of you, Boss, your
mind is so sharp. I wonder why.

153
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:11,220
Hey, Mokku!

154
00:15:13,289 --> 00:15:17,320
If you do that, the water will rush out
and the whole town will be in big trouble!

155
00:15:18,608 --> 00:15:19,680
What, you again?!

156
00:15:20,125 --> 00:15:23,260
Stop it, Mokku! Are you
trying to flood the whole town?!

157
00:15:23,521 --> 00:15:26,880
Shut up! I want legs! Legs that move!

158
00:15:30,473 --> 00:15:32,400
Hey, hurry it up!

159
00:15:32,645 --> 00:15:35,920
If the handle won't work, why
not try smashing it with a rock?

160
00:15:52,824 --> 00:15:56,547
I'm starving... I want food...

161
00:16:01,045 --> 00:16:03,140
Boss, it's raining.

162
00:16:03,628 --> 00:16:05,060
Shall we go?

163
00:16:06,475 --> 00:16:08,053
Where are you going?

164
00:16:08,859 --> 00:16:11,623
To take shelter from the
rain. I hate getting wet.

165
00:16:11,759 --> 00:16:13,239
Please tell me if you're leaving.

166
00:16:13,829 --> 00:16:17,475
You idiot! I haven't eaten
in ages, this is ridiculous!

167
00:16:30,329 --> 00:16:34,060
That Kenken... next time I
see him, he won't get off easy!

168
00:16:39,419 --> 00:16:43,500
The ants have it nice. Under the big
tree, not having to worry about the rain.

169
00:16:59,649 --> 00:17:02,471
I wonder if the floodgate is okay...
The spot where I hit it with the rock...

170
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:29,275
There's so much water...

171
00:17:46,009 --> 00:17:47,893
It's the spot where I
hit it with the rock...

172
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:56,127
It won't stop...

173
00:18:03,528 --> 00:18:07,200
As they say, even a massive dike
can collapse from a single ant hole.

174
00:18:07,584 --> 00:18:12,316
Even a sturdy dike can be
destroyed by one tiny ant hole!

175
00:18:15,249 --> 00:18:16,459
Grandpa!

176
00:18:23,109 --> 00:18:27,120
What are you dawdling for?!
Hurry up and plug the leak!

177
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:28,460
H-How?

178
00:18:29,059 --> 00:18:30,340
Stuff it with wood!

179
00:18:30,514 --> 00:18:32,100
Wood? There isn't any wood around here!

180
00:18:32,409 --> 00:18:34,220
Yes there is! You're made of wood!

181
00:18:34,514 --> 00:18:38,185
M-Me? You're telling me to use
my own body to stop the water?

182
00:18:38,769 --> 00:18:40,220
There's no other way!

183
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:41,679
No! I don't want to!

184
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:49,500
There it is!

185
00:18:51,899 --> 00:18:55,420
What are you messing around for?!
Hurry, or the floodgate will break!

186
00:18:56,054 --> 00:18:59,620
No way! If I lose these arms and
legs, there are no replacements!

187
00:18:59,725 --> 00:19:02,620
Fine! Then let the whole
town drown in water!

188
00:19:02,964 --> 00:19:04,777
Grandpa will just drown and die, too!

189
00:20:28,419 --> 00:20:30,632
Thank goodness, it held.

190
00:20:35,899 --> 00:20:36,768
Mokku!

191
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:39,965
Mokku...

192
00:20:48,149 --> 00:20:50,180
Mokku, you...

193
00:20:53,229 --> 00:20:57,840
You drove your own body into it for me...?

194
00:21:11,942 --> 00:21:15,720
Well, Grandpa is going
to go deliver this order.

195
00:21:55,429 --> 00:21:56,960
You are...

196
00:21:57,409 --> 00:22:03,844
Mokku, I saw everything. Your noble
deed. You did well to save the townspeople.

197
00:22:05,287 --> 00:22:12,039
You were magnificent. Truly magnificent.
I have come to give you life once again.

198
00:22:19,265 --> 00:22:20,265
I can move!

199
00:22:25,054 --> 00:22:28,620
Please, wait! How was I restored?

200
00:22:30,094 --> 00:22:33,637
You sacrificed your precious limbs to
save others.

201
00:22:35,426 --> 00:22:36,900
Compassion for people...

202
00:22:37,449 --> 00:22:39,371
...that is the feeling known as love.

203
00:22:40,582 --> 00:22:41,602
Your love...

204
00:22:42,129 --> 00:22:43,781
...has given you life. 

205
00:22:43,805 --> 00:22:45,520
My love did?

206
00:22:57,310 --> 00:22:58,000
Come on!

207
00:22:59,750 --> 00:23:01,400
Hey, that's dangerous!

208
00:23:01,665 --> 00:23:02,907
Sorry, sorry!

209
00:23:04,369 --> 00:23:05,437
Mokku!

210
00:23:06,912 --> 00:23:11,009
Look out if you're not paying
attention! We're in the middle of a match!

211
00:23:11,172 --> 00:23:12,916
Hey, Mokku!

212
00:23:12,939 --> 00:23:15,401
- Wait
- Hurry up Mokku!

213
00:23:15,839 --> 00:23:17,469
Nice going, Mokku!

214
00:23:33,969 --> 00:23:39,040
<i>Mokku becomes friends with Chikaro, a
monkey who can speak just like a human.</i>

215
00:23:40,029 --> 00:23:44,229
<i>Learning that Chikaro lives in a
wealthy mansion, Kenken and the others...</i>

216
00:23:44,254 --> 00:23:46,940
<i>...threaten Mokku to
make him bring them food.</i>

217
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:51,074
<i>However, when Mokku is
caught stealing the food...</i>

218
00:23:51,098 --> 00:23:53,972
<i>...he ends up chained
up along with Chikaro...</i>

219
00:23:53,997 --> 00:23:55,740
<i>...who is about to
be sold to a circus.</i>

220
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,980
<i>Look forward to next week's
Kashi no Ki Mokku!</i>

